title: Kubernetes::REST does not delegate load_yaml to its k8s attribute
updated: 2026-08-13T05:14:43Z
---

The k8s attribute in Kubernetes::REST delegates new_object, inflate, json_to_object, struct_to_object and expand_class, but not load_yaml -- so CLI::Cmd::Create has to reach through $api->k8s->load_yaml(...) to parse a YAML manifest, while the JSON sibling is just $api->inflate(...).

Adding load_yaml to that handles list is additive and would make the pair symmetric. REST.pm was outside the scope of #5 (another agent was working in it), hence this ticket rather than the change.

Note the argument contract if this is done: load_yaml parses characters, not bytes, unlike inflate whose decoder is utf8 => 1. A delegated load_yaml inherits that asymmetry, so it wants a line in the POD saying so.
